<title>PHILIPPINES: BPI cuts prime lending rate to 11.5 pct.</title>
<headline>BPI cuts prime lending rate to 11.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of the Philippine Islands said on Tuesday it had cut its prime lending to 11.5 percent from 12.0 percent a week ago.</p>
<p>Its &quot;super&quot; prime rate was likewise cut to 10.25 percent from 11.5 percent.</p>
<p>The prime lending rate is the interest rate charged by the bank to its top-tiered corporate clients.</p>
<p>The rate reduction comes after the benchmark 91-day treasury bill rate fell to an 18-month low of 9.724 percent on Monday due to excess liquidity.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
